    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 only one test class exists (`AcceptanceTest`; the other two files are helpers), and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the audit requirement for successful owner creation on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**New function class** \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated.java`:\n- Single responsibility: emits one line to the SLF4J logger named `AUDIT` (`LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`) containing the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`.\n- Reads the persisted entity via `@Val Owner`, following the existing state-passing convention.\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted an `audit` step between `save` and `respond`, so the owner's generated id is available (assigned during save) and the line is emitted only on the success path (any earlier escalation short-circuits before it).\n\nThe `AUDIT` log line confirmed in the test output: `AUDIT - owner created: id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-18`, and `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` passes.",
